  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a spike (e.g., >85) followed by immediate reversal; true outcomes consistently drop 10-15 points below the forecast in the first week.",
    "Forecast fails to account for mean reversion after sentiment spikes (0.40+); model assumes linear growth while actual prices trend sharply downward regardless of prior positive sentiment.",
    "Apply negative correction factor of -8% to -12% on 30-day horizon forecasts when the last 5 days show a price increase followed by at least one day of negative sentiment or flat sentiment.",
    "Model overestimates volatility recovery; true outcomes remain depressed for 2-3 weeks after an initial drop, whereas model predicts steady upward drift.",
    "When history ends with a high value (85+) and the next day is lower, reduce forecast by 10% immediately to avoid overshooting the subsequent trough."
  ]
}
